#       Source of truth for freminal's terminfo entry.  `cargo xtask terminfo`
#       compiles this file with `tic -x` into res/terminfo/ (letter and hex
#       layouts) and packs that tree into res/terminfo.tar.  Run it after every
#       edit to this file; building does not regenerate them.  Capabilities are
#       declared only where freminal implements them, with two standard key
#       capabilities as the exception: `kcbt` and `kent` are declared but not
#       sent by the input encoder (see DECLARED_NOT_SENT in
#       terminal_handler/dcs/terminfo_truth_tests.rs, which records why).  Every
#       value that the XTGETTCAP handler (`lookup_termcap` in
#       terminal_handler/dcs.rs) also answers must be identical to the one below;
#       a test enforces it.
#
#       This path is public.  The README links the file's raw URL on `main`,
#       https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fredsystems/freminal/main/res/freminal.ti,
#       for `curl ... | tic -x -`, so it must not move or be renamed.  The file is
#       also attached to every release and nightly as `freminal.ti`.
#
#       Deliberately absent because freminal does not implement them: `invis` and
#       the SGR 8 part of `sgr` (conceal is parsed but ignored, see
#       ESCAPE_SEQUENCE_GAPS.md) and `km` (Alt sends no 8th bit and there is no
#       ?1034).  `acsc` is the xterm-256color value (freminal prints `+ , - . 0 h`
#       as ASCII or U+2424, not as board glyphs).  Deliberately not declared
#       because their values are unverified: `RGB`, `xm`, `RV`, `is2`/`rs2` and
#       `smglp`/`smglr`/`smgrp`.
#
#       Extended (user-defined) capabilities are read from the xterm-256color,
#       xterm-kitty and foot entries, after checking the behaviour in freminal:
#       Tc/setrgbf/setrgbb (SGR 38/48;2), Ss/Se (DECSCUSR, 0 restores the
#       configured style), Ms (OSC 52), Cs/Cr (OSC 12/112), BD/BE/PS/PE (?2004),
#       fd/fe/kxIN/kxOUT/XF (?1004, CSI I / CSI O), E3 (CSI 3 J), XR (CSI > 0 q),
#       XM (?1000/?1006), Sync (?2026), smxx/rmxx (SGR 9/29), AX (SGR 39/49).
#       The modified-key families match the encoder in input.rs
#       (1 + shift + 2*alt + 4*ctrl, so 3..7 are Alt .. Ctrl+Alt).
#
#       Notification support (Task 76): Freminal handles OSC 9 (iTerm2/WezTerm)
#       and OSC 777 (urxvt "notify;TITLE;BODY") desktop notifications.  These
#       are one-way, fire-and-forget sequences with no capability-query
#       handshake, and terminfo defines no capability code for them, so there
#       is nothing to advertise here.  Programs detect Freminal at runtime via
#       TERM_PROGRAM=freminal (set in the PTY environment) rather than terminfo.
xterm-freminal|freminal|Freminal terminal emulator,
        am, bce, ccc, hs, mc5i, mir, msgr, npc, xenl, AX, Su, Tc, XF,
        colors#256, cols#80, it#8, lines#24, pairs#32767,
        acsc=``aaffggiijjkkllmmnnooppqqrrssttuuvvwwxxyyzz{{||}}~~,
        bel=^G, blink=\E[5m, bold=\E[1m, cbt=\E[Z, civis=\E[?25l,
        clear=\E[H\E[2J, cnorm=\E[?12l\E[?25h, cr=^M,
        csr=\E[%i%p1%d;%p2%dr, cub=\E[%p1%dD, cub1=^H,
        cud=\E[%p1%dB, cud1=^J, cuf=\E[%p1%dC, cuf1=\E[C,
        cup=\E[%i%p1%d;%p2%dH, cuu=\E[%p1%dA, cuu1=\E[A,
        cvvis=\E[?12;25h, dch=\E[%p1%dP, dch1=\E[P, dim=\E[2m,
        dl=\E[%p1%dM, dl1=\E[M, dsl=\E]2;\007, ech=\E[%p1%dX,
        ed=\E[J, el=\E[K, el1=\E[1K, flash=\E[?5h$<100/>\E[?5l,
        fsl=^G, home=\E[H, hpa=\E[%i%p1%dG, ht=^I, hts=\EH,
        ich=\E[%p1%d@, il=\E[%p1%dL, il1=\E[L, ind=^J,
